[CENTER][SIZE=6][B]Project Gielinor — Rust Server[/B][/SIZE]
[SIZE=4]Revision 239.1 • OpenRune content migration[/SIZE][/CENTER]

Project Gielinor is an in-progress Rust server project. The work started with networking, login, saved characters and a ticking world, then expanded into gameplay and OpenRune content.

This thread will follow the server’s development and the OpenRune content port.

The pictures include Rust-server sessions, scripted native-client tests and Kotlin reference comparisons. Test accounts have prepared items and levels.

[SIZE=4][B]OpenRune port progress[/B][/SIZE]
The ledger currently tracks 173 implementation units. Porting and testing continue alongside each other.

[TABLE]
[TR][TH]Area[/TH][TH]Ported so far[/TH][TH]Testing and next steps[/TH][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Herblore[/B][/TD][TD]Herb cleaning, unfinished/finished potion recipes, grinding, tar and dose upgrades.[/TD][TD]Native checks for selected recipes; more recipe and lifecycle tests to follow.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Food and drinks[/B][/TD][TD]Healing, multiple bites, returned containers, boosts and drink effects.[/TD][TD]Selected native food/drink checks passed; item coverage is expanding.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Cooking and preparation[/B][/TD][TD]Dough, pie/pizza assembly, fire and range recipes.[/TD][TD]Native dough and selected assembly runs passed; broader cooking checks continue.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Crafting[/B][/TD][TD]Gems, glassblowing, pottery, spinning, weaving, jewellery and leatherwork.[/TD][TD]Recipe and quantity tests in place; further native testing planned.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Mining and woodcutting[/B][/TD][TD]Ore/tree profiles, tool selection, depletion and respawn.[/TD][TD]Copper mining tested natively; wider node and tool checks continue.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Runecrafting[/B][/TD][TD]Selected rune altars, Daeyalt essence and outfit bonuses.[/TD][TD]World and selected native altar checks; reference work continues.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Prayer content[/B][/TD][TD]Bone burial, ash scattering and Zealot robe effects.[/TD][TD]Rule and world tests in place; further native/lifecycle checks remain.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Guilds and services[/B][/TD][TD]Tanning, guild access, deposit boxes, cape sales and worn Boost.[/TD][TD]Crafting-cape worn Boost independently verified; other services are being checked.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]NPC and item interactions[/B][/TD][TD]Pickpocketing, item packs, coin pouches, water filling and milking.[/TD][TD]Selected native item/service runs passed; wider interaction coverage continues.[/TD][/TR]
[TR][TD][B]Scenery and traversal[/B][/TD][TD]Searches, pickables, chests/drawers, ladders/stairs, signposts and spade Dig.[/TD][TD]Empty-search feature independently verified; newer handlers and quest Dig hooks are next.[/TD][/TR]
[/TABLE]

[SIZE=4][B]A Rust server you can log into[/B][/SIZE]
Rust handles the connection, world simulation, movement, player/NPC updates and character storage. Inventory, equipment and banking are connected to the gameplay runtime.

